---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';

const title = 'Rack & Pinion Actuator Manufacturer | Twin-Piston Quarter-Turn Factory | PNEUMACTUATOR';
const desc = 'PNEUMACTUATOR manufactures twin-piston rack and pinion pneumatic actuators in Wenzhou, China — compact AT-series units from 8 to 4,000+ Nm, ISO 5211 / NAMUR compliant, double acting and spring return, with OEM/ODM support for valve brands.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={desc}>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-navy-950 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-night-green">Manufacturer</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Rack &amp; Pinion Actuator Manufacturer</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-300">Twin-piston rack and pinion pneumatic actuators from a dedicated production line in Wenzhou: compact quarter-turn units from 8 Nm to 4,000+ Nm, hard-anodized aluminum bodies, ISO 5211 and NAMUR interfaces, and OEM/ODM support for valve distributors and automation brands.</p>
      <button type="button" data-quote-open class="mt-8 inline-block rounded-lg bg-cta-orange px-6 py-3 text-base font-semibold text-white shadow-lg transition hover:bg-orange-600">Request a Quote</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Factory advantages -->
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-blue">Why Buy Direct</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">The Rack &amp; Pinion Specialist Difference</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Most rack and pinion actuators on the market follow the same twin-piston layout; the differences show up in machining quality, seal selection and testing discipline. The AT line is built around those three points, and the sections below explain what that means for a valve distributor or automation integrator.</p>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-navy-950">Twin-Piston Mechanism, Machined In-House</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">The AT series uses two opposed pistons driving a common pinion, which balances the force on the output shaft and keeps the torque curve consistent across the 90° stroke. Racks and pinions are cut in our own machine shop rather than bought as finished parts, so tooth geometry, backlash and surface finish are controlled at the source. Pinion support and seal placement are arranged so that side loads from the valve stem stay away from the air chamber, which keeps leak performance stable over the life of the unit. The result is a compact package that fits in tight valve trains and delivers repeatable quarter-turn motion cycle after cycle.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-navy-950">Built for Long Service Life</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Bodies are hard-anodized aluminum (EN AC-44300) to resist corrosion in humid plant air, and the piston and pinion seals are sized for the 2–8 bar supply range used by most industrial plants. Travel stops allow ±5° adjustment so the stroke angle can be trimmed to the valve's open and closed positions. Spring return versions add a spring cartridge that pushes the pistons back to the fail position when air is vented, so the same AT frame serves both modulating and safety duties. Batch samples are endurance-cycled to 1,000,000 cycles, which is the design life target stated on the AT series datasheet.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-navy-950">OEM &amp; ODM for Valve Brands</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">A large share of our rack and pinion output leaves the factory under customer brands. Private label includes your logo, nameplate and packaging, while ODM work covers spring sets tuned to a specific torque curve, stroke angle changes, alternative coatings for coastal service, and mounting adaptations for non-standard valve patterns. Because the mechanism is machined in-house, a customer's torque curve can be matched without redesigning the body — spring selection, travel stops and coating changes are the levers, and they all sit inside our normal production flow. Drawings are issued for approval before batch production begins.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Product line table -->
  <section class="bg-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-blue">Product Line</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">AT Series Rack &amp; Pinion Range</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white">
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-navy-950 text-white">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-6 py-3.5 font-semibold">Parameter</th>
                <th class="px-6 py-3.5 font-semibold">AT Series Specification</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">
              <tr class="bg-white">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950">Output Torque</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">8 – 4,000+ Nm (double acting); spring return per model</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-50/60">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950">Rotation Angle</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">90° standard, adjustable ±5° with travel stops</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-white">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950">Supply Pressure</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">2 – 8 bar (29 – 116 psi)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-50/60">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950">Operating Temperature</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">−20°C to +80°C standard; −40°C to +150°C options</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-white">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950">Body Material</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Hard-anodized aluminum (EN AC-44300)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-50/60">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950">Mounting Standards</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">ISO 5211 (valve), NAMUR VDI/VDE 3845 (accessories)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-white">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950">Configurations</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Double acting / spring return (FC or FO)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-50/60">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950">Typical Valve Sizes</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">DN15 – DN300 ball, butterfly and plug valves</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-slate-400">* Torque values are reference figures at 5.5 bar. Combined with our AW scotch yoke line, the factory covers actuator torque from 8 Nm up to 200,000 Nm for valves up to DN1200.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Quality & torque testing -->
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-blue">Quality &amp; Testing</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">Torque Verification on Every Unit</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Rack and pinion actuators earn their reputation on torque accuracy and seal integrity. Every assembled AT-series unit is mounted on a calibrated torque rig and stroked in both directions while output is measured against the datasheet curve for the customer's operating pressure. Air leak tests at the rated supply pressure verify the piston seals, port threads and spring-cartridge O-rings before packing.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Endurance is verified at the batch level: representative samples are cycled to 1,000,000 cycles while torque output and leak rate are monitored at intervals. Dimensional checks on ISO 5211 mounting faces and the NAMUR pad use calibrated gauges, and hard-anodized coating condition is inspected on every body. Per-lot QC reports accompany each shipment, and material certificates are available on request.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Accessories are a common failure point on actuator packages, so the assembled stack — solenoid valve, limit switch box, filter regulator — is verified when we ship a complete package. Wiring, port thread sizes and the NAMUR interface are checked against the order before packing, which removes the classic parts-do-not-fit-at-site problem for distributors who source the whole assembly from one factory.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-navy-950">What We Test</h3>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
            <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-0.5 grid h-5 w-5 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-night-green/10 text-xs font-bold text-night-green">✓</span>Torque curve measurement in both directions at rated pressure</li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-0.5 grid h-5 w-5 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-night-green/10 text-xs font-bold text-night-green">✓</span>Air leak test at 2–8 bar depending on model</li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-0.5 grid h-5 w-5 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-night-green/10 text-xs font-bold text-night-green">✓</span>Full-stroke cycle check with travel stop adjustment</li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-0.5 grid h-5 w-5 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-night-green/10 text-xs font-bold text-night-green">✓</span>ISO 5211 / NAMUR dimensional inspection</li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-0.5 grid h-5 w-5 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-night-green/10 text-xs font-bold text-night-green">✓</span>1,000,000-cycle endurance test on batch samples</li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-0.5 grid h-5 w-5 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-night-green/10 text-xs font-bold text-night-green">✓</span>Anodized coating and surface finish inspection</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Applications -->
  <section class="bg-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-blue">Applications</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">Where Rack &amp; Pinion Actuators Are Used</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">The compact envelope and predictable torque curve make twin-piston rack and pinion actuators the standard choice for automating quarter-turn valves up to DN300 in plant and pipeline service.</p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        <a href="/industries/butterfly-valves/" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-navy-950 shadow-sm transition hover:border-brand-blue hover:text-brand-blue">Butterfly Valve Automation</a>
        <a href="/industries/ball-valves/" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-navy-950 shadow-sm transition hover:border-brand-blue hover:text-brand-blue">Ball Valve Automation</a>
        <span class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 shadow-sm">Plug Valves &amp; Dampers</span>
        <a href="/industries/water-treatment/" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-navy-950 shadow-sm transition hover:border-brand-blue hover:text-brand-blue">Water &amp; Wastewater</a>
        <a href="/industries/oil-gas/" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-navy-950 shadow-sm transition hover:border-brand-blue hover:text-brand-blue">Oil &amp; Gas Pipelines</a>
        <a href="/industries/chemical-processing/" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-navy-950 shadow-sm transition hover:border-brand-blue hover:text-brand-blue">Chemical Processing</a>
        <span class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 shadow-sm">HVAC &amp; Building Automation</span>
        <span class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 shadow-sm">Food &amp; Beverage</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-blue">FAQ</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">Rack &amp; Pinion Actuator Manufacturer — FAQ</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
        <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-bold text-navy-950">Why choose rack and pinion over scotch yoke?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Rack and pinion actuators are more compact and cost-effective for valves up to about DN300, and their balanced twin-piston design delivers a consistent torque profile across the stroke. Scotch yoke actuators generate higher torque at the end positions, which matters for large valves with high breakout requirements. Our engineers will recommend one or the other based on your valve size, pressure class and torque curve.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-bold text-navy-950">What torque range do your rack and pinion actuators cover?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">The AT series covers 8–4,000+ Nm in double acting configuration, with spring return torque specified per model. When a project exceeds the rack and pinion range, our scotch yoke line extends coverage to 200,000+ Nm, so the factory can supply the complete torque spread.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-bold text-navy-950">Do you offer spring return versions for fail-safe operation?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Yes. AT-series rack and pinion actuators are available as spring return units that move the valve to a fail position (closed or open) when air supply is lost. Spring sets can be selected and pre-loaded to match your valve's seating torque requirement, and adjustments are possible after installation.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-bold text-navy-950">Can you private label rack and pinion actuators for our brand?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Yes. Private label includes your logo, nameplate and packaging, and we can adapt spring sets, stroke angles, coatings and mounting interfaces for your valve range. After sample approval, batch production typically runs in 7–15 days for standard configurations. Contact sales@pneumactuator.com with your volume for a quotation.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Match an Actuator to Your Valve"
    subtitle="Send the valve type, size, torque requirement and fail-safe position — we reply with a rack and pinion recommendation and factory-direct pricing within 24 hours."
  />
</Layout>
